{"text": "From: Renczkowski, Daniel (OPH)\n\nse Friday, October 06, 2006 9:25 AM\nTo: khan, Annie (OPH); Salemi, Charles (OPH); Saunders, Della (OPH); O\u2019Brien, Elisabeth\n(OPH); Corbett, Kate (OPH); Tran, Mai (OPH): Medina, Nicole (OPH)\nSubject: FW: Dateline DEA - October 6, 2006\n\nCheck out this link if nothing else:\n\nhitlo:/ww justthinktwice.com/stumbleweed/home. htm!\n\nFrom: dateline_dea-bounced@vdcserver01.usdo}.gov [mailto:dateline_dea-bounced@wdcserver01.usdol.gov] On\nBehalf Of owner-dateline dea@vdcserver01.usd0}.d0v\nSent: Friday, October 06, 2006 8:46 AM\nTo: dateline dea@wdcserver01.usdol.gov\nSubject: Dateline DEA - October 6, 2006\n\nDEA's Biweekly E-mail Informant\n\nOctober 6, 2006\n\nLeaders of the Infamous Cali Cartel Plead Guilty\n\nMiguel and Gilberto Rodriguez-Orejuela, brothers who ran the powerful Cali Cartel in Colombia that was\nresponsible for importing tons of cocaine into the United States over the last two decades, have pleaded guilty\ntoa charge of conspiracy to import cocaine into the United States. \"The Rodriguez-Orejuela brothers defined\nthe label \"kingpin,\" said Administrator Karen P. Tandy. \"During little more than a decade, their Cali cartel\nsold at least 30,000 kilos of cocaine and amassed an illicit fortune worth in excess of SI billion.\"\n\nClick here for the Press Release\n\nlick here for more about the history of the Ce\n\nSearch Warrants Served at San Francisco Marijuana Distribution Center\n\nDEA made 15 arrests and seized a sophisticated indoor marijuana grow and thousands of marijuana plants. As\npart of the investigation against Remedies Cooperative LLC, (formerly known as Compassionate Caregivers)\nand Potent Employment Solutions, agents also seized 2 vehicles, including a Porsche Carrera convertible, and a\ntotal of $125,000 in U.S. Currency . \"Federal drug laws prohibit the cultivation and sale of marijuana. Anyone\n\nCorbett_email_PRR_025493,",
